<article class="env-lemma" id="0C8N">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C8N">Lemma <span data-tag="0C8N">55.5.15</span>.</a> Nonexistence of proper subgraphs of the form </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \bullet \ar@{-}[r] &  \bullet \ar@{-}[r] &  \bullet \ar@{-}[r] &  \bullet \ar@{-}[r] \ar@{-}[d] &  \bullet \ar@{-}[r] &  \bullet \ar@{-}[r] &  \bullet \\  &  &  &  \bullet }  \]
</div>
  <p> Assume $n > 8$. There do <strong>not</strong> exist $8$ distinct $(-2)$-indices $e, f, g, h, i, j, k, l$ such that $a_{ef}, a_{fg}, a_{gh}, a_{hi}, a_{ij}, a_{jk}, a_{lh}$ are nonzero. </p>
